{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the seventh day, etc.</b> That is, by your making a Sabbath for HaShem — in this you make HaShem your Elohim, in the manner our Sages of blessed memory said (Exodus Rabbah 25) that the Sabbath is equal to the entire Torah. Or perhaps the entire Torah is alluded to in the word שַׁבָּת in the following manner: there are 611 commandments that they did not hear from the mouth of the Almighty but from the mouth of a prophet, and two commandments, ״אָנֹכִי״ and ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״, which are the two commandments that they were commanded from the mouth of the Almighty — the commandment of ״אָנֹכִי״ is a positive commandment, and ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״ is a negative commandment. Now our Rabbis of blessed memory have already informed us that positive commandments are refined in the name of the attribute of Mercy, because they are in the aspect of receiving reward, and negative commandments are refined in the name of Adonai, because they are in the aspect of Justice for one who transgresses them. And behold, the numerical value of יהוה and אדני totals 91, plus 611 — here is שַׁבָּת [i.e., equals the word's value, 702]." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in the manner of what they said in tractate Shabbat (Shabbat 118a): Whoever observes the Sabbath according to its laws — even if he worships idolatry like Enosh — his sins are forgiven him. And this is what the verse says: <b>and the seventh day is a Sabbath to HaShem</b> — through this He becomes your <b>Elohim</b> and no other. You have thus learned that he is forgiven for having accepted a god other than Him, blessed be He." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in its saying <b>a Sabbath to HaShem</b>: that the rest and the cessation are not to be for your own repose and leisure, but rather for the commandment of HaShem his Elohim." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in this manner: <b>Six days you shall labor</b>, etc. — <b>and the seventh day</b> shall also have for you one labor. And what is it? That you make a Sabbath to HaShem your Elohim. And I did not diminish for you the seventh day except from your own work."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:05.139420042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}